fof_version: '1.0'
type: enemy
id: archive_guardian
name: Archive Guardian
ruleset:
  modules:
  - id: base
    version: 1.0.0
enemy:
  # v0.3: Boss, durability 8, attack +3, heavy armor, phase change, rating 16 — the top of the old ladder.
  level: 5
  role: boss
  armor: 2
  morale: 12
  weapon: Iron hands, and seven feet of weight behind them
  wants: The archive undisturbed, and nothing else.
  special: THE JOINTS — it was built by people, so it has joints. Each time a character lands
    a 10+ and takes a stunt aimed at one, its attack bonus drops by 1 for the rest of the
    fight, to a minimum of 0. The party discovers this in play; the MM does not announce it.
  when_bloodied: Reduced Mode. Whatever was weighing consequences shuts down, and what is
    left is more dangerous. Every hit it lands is a hard hit, and it fixes on whoever last
    hurt it and does not look away until one of them is finished. It is running on something
    else now. What that is, the party does not know.
  tells: Seven feet of iron-jointed patience, with eyes that make light instead of catching
    it. It walks the same line across the room, at the same pace, and it does not hurry.
  breaks: Never breaks; it was not built with any. It stops when it is destroyed or when the
    thing it guards is no longer in the room, and it lets anyone leave empty-handed by the
    door they came in through.
  twists:
  - 'One arm no longer answers it: one attack an exchange, not two, until it is bloodied.'
  - What it guarded was removed years ago. It is guarding an empty room and does not know.
  - Its patrol is fixed to the minute, and a party that watches first can walk through the
    gap.
  - A door on the far side can be sealed, shutting it in with the thing it guards.
  - Somebody came before the party and did not leave, and their notes are on the floor.
  - The floor is failing under fifteen years of its weight, and the right blow in the right
    place sends it through.
  nastier: Reduced Mode starts at the first hit that lands on a joint, not at half HP.
  description: >-
    A Constructed guardian commissioned by the Thornwall city government through the Artificers'
    Guild, designed to hold a fixed position and prevent unauthorized access. Standing approximately
    seven feet tall, iron-jointed, with eyes that produce rather than reflect light. It has
    been in this room for fifteen years with no instructions other than the original ones.

    It is not malevolent. It is doing exactly what it was told. That is, in certain lights,
    worse.
  notes: >-
    Level 5 Boss, armor 2: no overrides. The highest-level card in the Bestiary on purpose:
    against a level 1–2 party its level gap makes every attack Hard, which is the numbers
    saying what the entry has always said.


    Intended to be solved laterally: structural weaknesses, its fixed patrol logic, a sealed
    door, the joints. A straight fight is survivable but very expensive. The joint weakness
    is the v0.3 joint rule, restated as a stunt on a 10+.


    Its phase is the v0.3 Reduced Mode (re-authored 2026-09-08, R2/D20), restated for hard
    hits: the Guardian stops being careful the moment something finally tells it that something
    is wrong.


    Appears: one, in the room it was built to hold.
  reskin_of: null
